# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# This file must live at the CONTEXT ROOT to take effect. The image is built with
# `context: .` and `file: src/Dockerfile` (.github/workflows/docker-image-build.yaml),
# and BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` then `<context>/.dockerignore` —
# never `src/.dockerignore`. An earlier ignore file lived at src/.dockerignore and was
# therefore never read, which is why test files were shipping inside the image.
#
# Deliberately minimal. The Dockerfile already copies only the three things it needs
# (src/butler-sheet-icons.js, src/globals.js, src/lib/), so a broad exclusion list adds
# no value and adds risk: the old src/.dockerignore excluded package-lock.json, which
# would have broken `npm ci` in the deps stage had it ever been read.
#
# Keep in step with `COPY src/lib/ ./src/lib/` in src/Dockerfile — that line is the only
# reason anything under src/lib/ needs excluding at all.

# Unit and integration tests: ~48 files with no purpose at runtime.
**/__tests__/
**/*.test.js

# Shared test fixtures. These live outside __tests__/ so Jest's default discovery does not
# claim them as suites, which means neither rule above catches them — and engine-mocks.js
# imports @jest/globals, a devDependency `npm ci --omit=dev` never installs.
**/test-helpers/
